# SYNOPSIS

```text
protocol todhchai.auth.AuthSession version 1
call next() throws(AuthError) -> Step
call feed(message: [UInt8]) throws(AuthError)
call failure() -> String
event answered()
```

# DESCRIPTION

Protocol `todhchai.auth.AuthSession`, version 1, of library `AuthIPC`, its messages in the one wire format (wire(6)).

| Method | Kind | Since | Ordinal |
| `next` | call | 1 | `0x67ef3e01b5a5a1ae` |
| `feed` | call | 1 | `0x3d25bc432d1dbdbb` |
| `failure` | call | 1 | `0x34c1621c59540ad7` |
| `answered` | event | 1 | `0x58fe95882c6d8170` |

: `failure`
  Why the session failed (the peer's error, in words).
: `answered`
  The user answered what a `needKey` or `needConfirm` step asked.

